<Wizard::IntroContent
  @imageAlt="Entity and alias structure showing how authentication methods map to a single entity with associated policies"
  @imageCaption="An entity is made up of aliases that map individual authentication methods to a single entity. Policies are then tied to an entity."
  @imageSrc={{img-path "~/entities-intro.png"}}
>
  <:description>
    Entities
    <strong>unify a client's identity across multiple authentication methods</strong>
    into a single representative in Vault. Each entity is made of one or more aliases, individual account mappings that link
    an auth method to the entity.
  </:description>
  <:features>
    <Wizard::IntroContent::Feature @icon="service">
      Entities consolidate identities across authentication methods, ensuring
      <strong>consistent policy enforcement</strong>
      and
      <strong>accurate client count</strong>
      tracking.
    </Wizard::IntroContent::Feature>
    <Wizard::IntroContent::Feature @icon="database">
      Entities are
      <strong>scoped to the namespaces</strong>
      where the client authenticates. They may extend to child namespaces, but do not apply cluster-wide by default.
    </Wizard::IntroContent::Feature>
    <Wizard::IntroContent::Feature @icon="org">
      Though entities are automatically created upon first login,
      <strong>operators should still explicitly manage and merge them</strong>
      to avoid duplicates and inflated client counts.
    </Wizard::IntroContent::Feature>
  </:features>
</Wizard::IntroContent>